1
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:40,039
[River of No Return]

2
00:01:40,090 --> 00:01:43,000
[Episode 14: Mud]

3
00:01:53,690 --> 00:01:54,420
Sick Madman.

4
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:56,320
You're one tough bastard.

5
00:01:56,450 --> 00:01:58,310
Even that fire couldn't kill you.

6
00:01:58,970 --> 00:02:00,810
Save your strength.

7
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:02,340
I'll deal with you last.

8
00:02:05,140 --> 00:02:07,940
I have to deal with him first.

9
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:15,970
Sick Madman!

10
00:02:17,650 --> 00:02:19,180
I'm the one you want to kill.

11
00:02:19,410 --> 00:02:20,540
Come straight at me.

12
00:02:22,570 --> 00:02:23,530
And me!

13
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:35,120
Again!

14
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:18,300
Your Highness.

15
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:19,160
Your Highness!

16
00:04:27,430 --> 00:04:27,960
Catch!

17
00:05:53,659 --> 00:05:54,659
Your Highness...

18
00:05:57,300 --> 00:05:58,159
Your Highness!

19
00:06:06,770 --> 00:06:07,700
Little Xingren!

20
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:09,690
Rectifier Yu!

21
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:23,420
♪ Heading north a thousand miles,
treading the surging waves ♪

22
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:28,060
♪ Fierce winds and driving rain
don't matter ♪

23
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:30,410
♪ Undercurrents surge,
sails sway and toss ♪

24
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:32,890
♪ Even with inescapable traps
set all around ♪

25
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:37,180
♪ I insist on bringing clarity back
to this world ♪

26
00:06:38,150 --> 00:06:41,900
♪ Northward, the canal winds through
the vast unknown ♪

27
00:06:42,890 --> 00:06:46,600
♪ The lives along its banks
stir my soul ♪

28
00:06:46,890 --> 00:06:49,180
♪ Mountains may fall,
seas may be crossed ♪

29
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,650
♪ Though we sail together,
our paths may part ♪

30
00:06:51,670 --> 00:06:56,210
♪ Still, we'll forge
a new chapter for the Ming Empire ♪

31
00:07:04,110 --> 00:07:06,110
You've got some real perseverance.

32
00:07:13,690 --> 00:07:14,370
Old Mule!

33
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:15,730
It's up to your fate now!

34
00:08:19,450 --> 00:08:20,250
Young Master?

35
00:08:23,890 --> 00:08:24,750
Your Highness?

36
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:29,900
Your Highness?

37
00:08:32,090 --> 00:08:33,970
Just give me some sign, anything!

38
00:09:46,110 --> 00:09:46,970
Dingyuan.

39
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:49,590
You'll soon be reunited with your father.

40
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:51,680
He went ahead of you.

41
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:56,240
That look on your face
really reminds me of him.

42
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:58,900
How dare you even mention my father?

43
00:10:01,490 --> 00:10:02,420
You know,

44
00:10:03,390 --> 00:10:07,380
back then, Tie Xuan led his troops
up the mountain to suppress the bandits.

45
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:10,020
After that, I joined his ranks.

46
00:10:10,310 --> 00:10:11,720
At the battle of Dongchang,

47
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:13,900
I charged straight into
the Yan Army's formation.

48
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,300
No one could stop me.

49
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:17,810
Tie Xuan refused to surrender

50
00:10:17,810 --> 00:10:19,850
and was sentenced to a gruesome execution.

51
00:10:19,850 --> 00:10:20,570
Dingyuan.

52
00:10:22,710 --> 00:10:24,910
There was nothing I could do to save him.

53
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:26,900
I could only

54
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:30,490
stand by and watch him die.

55
00:10:33,690 --> 00:10:35,090
Whatever happened
between you and Tie Xuan,

56
00:10:35,090 --> 00:10:36,180
take it up with him.

57
00:10:36,210 --> 00:10:38,140
I don't want to hear your rambling.

58
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:46,000
Later, I went back to Jinling

59
00:10:46,570 --> 00:10:48,170
to rescue the lord's family,

60
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:49,740
but I failed again.

61
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:52,520
I was trapped on the mountain,

62
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:53,900
where I ran into your father.

63
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:55,430
Zhong Eryong recognized me

64
00:10:56,310 --> 00:10:57,610
and found a way

65
00:10:57,760 --> 00:10:58,970
to save my life.

66
00:11:00,060 --> 00:11:00,940
Dingyuan.

67
00:11:07,810 --> 00:11:10,490
But you've repeatedly ruined

68
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:13,170
the assignments the Alliance Leader
gave me,

69
00:11:14,190 --> 00:11:17,120
letting the Crown Prince escape
time and time again.

70
00:11:20,610 --> 00:11:22,230
There's a young girl among you

71
00:11:22,230 --> 00:11:23,630
who calls herself Envoy.

72
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:26,660
She said I was the one
you were looking for

73
00:11:26,970 --> 00:11:28,500
and even offered to save me.

74
00:11:28,570 --> 00:11:30,470
Yet here you are, trying to kill me.

75
00:11:30,470 --> 00:11:32,000
Aren't you on the same side?

76
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:34,310
Have you got the wrong person?

77
00:11:34,310 --> 00:11:35,210
Wu Dingyuan.

78
00:11:35,370 --> 00:11:37,030
I can't let you get away again.

79
00:11:37,470 --> 00:11:38,940
This might hurt a little,

80
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:40,260
so bear with it.

81
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:42,550
If it weren't for our past ties,

82
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:44,440
I'd have dealt with you long ago.

83
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:45,730
This ends today.

84
00:11:46,230 --> 00:11:47,960
There's no escaping your fate.

85
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:51,940
You let the Crown Prince escape

86
00:11:52,370 --> 00:11:54,490
and ruined the Alliance Leader's
grand plan.

87
00:11:54,490 --> 00:11:56,990
I've never forgotten
what your father did for me,

88
00:11:56,990 --> 00:11:58,650
but you're getting in the way.

89
00:11:58,940 --> 00:12:00,340
Don't hold it against me.

90
00:12:00,370 --> 00:12:01,970
Once this matter is settled,

91
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:04,720
I'll go to your father's grave
and ask for his forgiveness.

92
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:05,670
Liang Xingfu,

93
00:12:06,810 --> 00:12:07,610
seriously,

94
00:12:08,970 --> 00:12:11,770
will you shut up already?
You're driving me crazy.

95
00:12:12,110 --> 00:12:13,260
I'm sick of hearing you talk!

96
00:12:13,260 --> 00:12:14,670
I'm so fed up right now!

97
00:12:15,340 --> 00:12:16,810
Just take that knife in your hand

98
00:12:16,810 --> 00:12:17,980
and stab me!

99
00:12:18,970 --> 00:12:20,300
Go on, kill me! Hurry up!

100
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:35,180
Liang Xingfu!

101
00:12:35,450 --> 00:12:36,070
Stop!

102
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:41,020
[Zuo Yehe, Envoy of the Iron Alliance]

103
00:12:40,230 --> 00:12:41,730
I knew you weren't dead.

104
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:43,040
Envoy.

105
00:12:43,540 --> 00:12:44,610
I can't die yet.

106
00:12:44,810 --> 00:12:48,410
The Crown Prince is still alive,
and our mission isn't complete.

107
00:12:48,470 --> 00:12:49,600
Get him out of there.

108
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:51,910
I have to take care of him first.

109
00:12:52,090 --> 00:12:52,900
Get over here!

110
00:12:53,850 --> 00:12:56,450
Do you realize what a huge mistake
you've made?

111
00:12:56,660 --> 00:12:57,880
If I hadn't arrived in time,

112
00:12:57,880 --> 00:13:00,100
you would've ruined
our Iron Alliance's entire plan!

113
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:01,830
Our Leader's letter was clear:

114
00:13:01,940 --> 00:13:04,370
protect Wu Dingyuan at all costs

115
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:06,200
and bring him to Jinan alive.

116
00:13:06,430 --> 00:13:07,680
I told you back in Jinling

117
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:08,940
not to act recklessly.

118
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:12,900
Can you please start listening to me
from now on?

119
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:27,700
I'll listen to you.

120
00:13:28,110 --> 00:13:29,310
Let's go back to Jinan

121
00:13:30,300 --> 00:13:31,630
and receive new orders.

122
00:13:34,990 --> 00:13:36,320
It's an alliance order,

123
00:13:36,560 --> 00:13:37,360
so I must obey.

124
00:13:38,020 --> 00:13:40,550
Let's go to Jinan
and see the Alliance Leader.

125
00:13:41,330 --> 00:13:42,130
Little Envoy.

126
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:43,470
I'm not going to Jinan.

127
00:13:43,470 --> 00:13:44,660
I'm definitely not going to Jinan.

128
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:46,000
I'm going back to Jinling. I'm going...

129
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,140
If you don't want to go to Jinan,

130
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:48,540
let's go to Huai'an then.

131
00:13:49,550 --> 00:13:50,150
Huai'an?

132
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:52,210
Alright, alright. Anywhere else is fine.

133
00:13:52,210 --> 00:13:53,940
I just don't want to go to Jinan.

134
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:57,790
[Huai'an Branch of
the Ministry of Justice]

135
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:03,880
Open the door!

136
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:08,640
Who is it?

137
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:12,020
You filthy beggar!

138
00:14:12,110 --> 00:14:13,130
Do you have a death wish?

139
00:14:13,130 --> 00:14:14,790
Why is the prefectural office

140
00:14:14,990 --> 00:14:16,590
closed in broad daylight?

141
00:14:16,690 --> 00:14:17,540
Do you even know what place this is,

142
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:18,740
barging in like that?

143
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:22,180
The Huai'an Branch of
the Ministry of Justice.

144
00:14:22,180 --> 00:14:24,350
Officially, it falls under the Ministry's
jurisdiction, but in practice,

145
00:14:24,350 --> 00:14:26,610
it functions as a subordinate office
of the Canal Transport Commander.

146
00:14:26,610 --> 00:14:28,690
It handles criminal cases
related to the canal.

147
00:14:28,690 --> 00:14:29,950
Is that correct or not!

148
00:14:30,730 --> 00:14:32,540
W-What business do you have here?

149
00:14:32,540 --> 00:14:34,000
I want to file a complaint.

150
00:14:34,070 --> 00:14:34,620
Hold it!

151
00:14:35,930 --> 00:14:37,440
Don't you know what time it is?

152
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:39,240
Who comes here during mealtime?

153
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:42,330
Canal transport runs day and night.

154
00:14:42,330 --> 00:14:43,900
There should always be
a judicial commissioner

155
00:14:43,900 --> 00:14:45,140
on duty in the courtroom.

156
00:14:45,140 --> 00:14:46,060
You're right,

157
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:47,940
but today's circumstances are unusual.

158
00:14:47,940 --> 00:14:49,140
No one's on duty here.

159
00:14:49,490 --> 00:14:51,020
And what makes today so unusual?

160
00:14:51,020 --> 00:14:52,420
Where has everyone gone?

161
00:14:53,570 --> 00:14:54,900
Where are they?

162
00:14:55,070 --> 00:14:56,780
Lord Wang Teng, Deputy Commander
of the Huai'an Guard...

163
00:14:56,780 --> 00:14:58,840
He... He's hosting a family banquet.

164
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:06,360
[Wang Teng, Deputy Commander
of the Huai'an Guard]

165
00:15:06,380 --> 00:15:09,350
[Fang Du, Judicial Commissioner of
the Ministry of Justice Branch]

166
00:15:06,450 --> 00:15:07,580
Come on, have a seat.

167
00:15:12,690 --> 00:15:15,490
It's only been 2 years.
Look how tall you've grown.

168
00:15:15,970 --> 00:15:16,570
Master.

169
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:18,260
All the expected guests have arrived.

170
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:19,560
Alright. Serve the food.

171
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:20,490
Serve the food!

172
00:15:24,910 --> 00:15:25,890
Come on, sit.

173
00:15:26,220 --> 00:15:27,020
Have a seat.

174
00:15:26,670 --> 00:15:28,670
[In Memory of Celestial Maiden,
Wang Jingshu]

175
00:15:31,450 --> 00:15:32,710
Ladies and gentlemen.

176
00:15:32,810 --> 00:15:34,070
My daughter, Jingshu,

177
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:36,700
was posthumously bestowed
the title of Celestial Maiden.

178
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:39,280
I've arranged this family banquet today
in her honor.

179
00:15:39,280 --> 00:15:41,940
She was intelligent and gentle
from a young age,

180
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:43,940
but sadly, her life was cut short.

181
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:47,330
As her father,

182
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:48,120
all I can do is

183
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:50,710
hold this modest banquet
to express my grief.

184
00:15:50,710 --> 00:15:53,710
I'm deeply grateful to
all the family and friends here

185
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:55,740
who have taken the time to attend.

186
00:15:56,610 --> 00:15:59,140
-It's only right.
-It's the least we could do.

187
00:16:01,330 --> 00:16:02,260
Come on. Come on.

188
00:16:19,250 --> 00:16:20,380
Commissioner Fang.

189
00:16:21,800 --> 00:16:22,840
We keep things simple here.

190
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:24,020
Just some light food and drinks.

191
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:25,110
I hope you'll forgive the humble fare.

192
00:16:25,110 --> 00:16:26,810
Lord Wang, as you're experiencing
a mix of joy and sorrow,

193
00:16:26,810 --> 00:16:27,610
all I can do...

194
00:16:29,570 --> 00:16:30,450
Come on, here.

195
00:16:39,140 --> 00:16:40,160
Commissioner Fang.

196
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:41,690
Someone is looking for you outside.

197
00:16:41,690 --> 00:16:42,450
Me?

198
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,960
Yu... Yu Tingyi?

199
00:16:54,990 --> 00:16:56,000
Fang Du?

200
00:16:57,920 --> 00:16:59,210
Tingyi!

201
00:17:01,090 --> 00:17:02,290
The constable told me

202
00:17:02,590 --> 00:17:04,050
the judicial commissioner on duty

203
00:17:04,050 --> 00:17:05,819
was attending a banquet
at Commander Wang's residence.

204
00:17:05,819 --> 00:17:07,490
So he was talking about you.

205
00:17:10,119 --> 00:17:10,859
Back then,

206
00:17:11,210 --> 00:17:13,319
we both placed among the top three
in the imperial examinations.

207
00:17:13,319 --> 00:17:15,190
I later joined the Messenger's Office
in Jinling.

208
00:17:15,190 --> 00:17:17,450
I never expected you'd end up in Huai'an.

209
00:17:19,190 --> 00:17:19,770
Tingyi,

210
00:17:20,290 --> 00:17:21,770
allow me to bow in gratitude.

211
00:17:21,770 --> 00:17:22,829
What's this about?

212
00:17:23,550 --> 00:17:24,970
If you hadn't stood up for me
outside the examination hall

213
00:17:24,970 --> 00:17:27,079
during the metropolitan examination,

214
00:17:27,079 --> 00:17:28,010
would I, Fang Du,

215
00:17:28,290 --> 00:17:29,550
ever have earned the title of jinshi?

216
00:17:29,550 --> 00:17:30,610
That was years ago.

217
00:17:30,860 --> 00:17:31,970
Let's not bring it up.

218
00:17:31,970 --> 00:17:33,210
We must. We must.

219
00:17:34,270 --> 00:17:37,470
A drop of kindness deserves a fountain
of gratitude in return.

220
00:17:37,470 --> 00:17:38,530
By the way, Tingyi,

221
00:17:38,950 --> 00:17:40,660
why are you in such a sorry state?

222
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:42,060
Where have you come from?

223
00:17:45,010 --> 00:17:45,730
I...

224
00:17:46,530 --> 00:17:47,860
I've come from Jinling.

225
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,940
Jin... Jinling?

226
00:17:51,490 --> 00:17:53,750
I do have an important favor
to ask of you.

227
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:55,970
Tingyi,

228
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:58,190
I heard the Crown Prince's treasure ship
was blown up.

229
00:17:58,190 --> 00:17:59,520
What exactly happened?

230
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:00,710
What have you heard?

231
00:18:02,250 --> 00:18:04,450
A turtledove steals the magpie's nest.

232
00:18:04,970 --> 00:18:07,440
Jinling has been rocked by a series of
upheavals in recent months.

233
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:08,550
The Crown Prince's ship was mysteriously

234
00:18:08,550 --> 00:18:10,480
blown up before it could even dock.

235
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:12,210
I also heard

236
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:15,390
that a palace eunuch suddenly
turned on everyone

237
00:18:15,770 --> 00:18:17,370
and killed the Crown Prince.

238
00:18:21,140 --> 00:18:22,740
That's what I've heard, too.

239
00:18:22,860 --> 00:18:24,410
That's why the people of Jinling

240
00:18:24,410 --> 00:18:25,870
are now in a state of panic.

241
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:28,340
But some say

242
00:18:30,420 --> 00:18:31,880
the Crown Prince might not

243
00:18:33,380 --> 00:18:34,380
actually be dead.

244
00:18:35,100 --> 00:18:36,700
The Crown Prince is not dead?

245
00:18:38,490 --> 00:18:39,620
That can't be right.

246
00:18:39,730 --> 00:18:41,320
This must be the work of
treacherous conspirators.

247
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:42,470
Our state is in peril.

248
00:18:42,470 --> 00:18:44,800
What were those 10 years of
hard study for?

249
00:18:45,010 --> 00:18:46,940
Wasn't it so that one day we could

250
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:48,970
serve the people, bring peace to the land,

251
00:18:48,970 --> 00:18:50,300
and set the world right?

252
00:18:51,150 --> 00:18:51,700
I...

253
00:19:14,550 --> 00:19:15,750
What did you just say?

254
00:19:16,290 --> 00:19:17,730
I... I just...

255
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:19,900
I just said...

256
00:19:20,210 --> 00:19:21,340
Set the world right.

257
00:19:26,490 --> 00:19:28,100
Come on, eat up. Please.

258
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:30,160
Master. Master.

259
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:37,220
Master, there's been an incident
at the dam.

260
00:19:37,220 --> 00:19:39,220
A 400-liao grain ship from Yangzhou

261
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:40,980
had its mooring rope snapped

262
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:42,120
while passing through the dam

263
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:43,150
and drifted out of the dock.

264
00:19:43,150 --> 00:19:44,130
It's caused quite a commotion.

265
00:19:44,130 --> 00:19:44,730
Nonsense!

266
00:19:45,010 --> 00:19:46,210
Do you know what day it is?

267
00:19:46,210 --> 00:19:48,250
I have no time to concern myself
with what's happening at the dam.

268
00:19:48,250 --> 00:19:49,410
Let the subordinate officials handle it.

269
00:19:49,410 --> 00:19:50,350
Don't bother me with this again.

270
00:19:50,350 --> 00:19:51,080
Yes, Master.

271
00:19:55,790 --> 00:19:57,380
My beloved daughter, Jingshu,

272
00:19:57,380 --> 00:19:59,780
had been bright and clever
from a young age.

273
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:03,040
I've always treasured her

274
00:20:04,050 --> 00:20:06,420
and protected her carefully.

275
00:20:07,190 --> 00:20:08,770
A girl like her

276
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:11,650
should have married into
an ordinary family,

277
00:20:11,820 --> 00:20:13,080
observed her wifely duties,

278
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:15,810
and devoted herself
to her husband and children.

279
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:16,900
But fate

280
00:20:17,340 --> 00:20:18,530
had other plans.

281
00:20:18,970 --> 00:20:21,970
Through blessings accumulated
over many lifetimes,

282
00:20:22,550 --> 00:20:26,610
she was granted the honor of serving
the late Emperor in his mausoleum...

283
00:20:27,360 --> 00:20:28,580
I've digressed.

284
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:32,450
Jingshu understood the greater good

285
00:20:32,450 --> 00:20:35,660
and brought generations of prosperity
and glory to our Wang family.

286
00:20:35,660 --> 00:20:36,290
So...

287
00:20:36,890 --> 00:20:40,370
This toast is not to her departed soul,

288
00:20:41,420 --> 00:20:43,680
but to the grace she has bestowed upon us.

289
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:55,320
My father has been reassigned
to the north.

290
00:20:54,510 --> 00:20:57,420
[Young Su Jingxi]

291
00:20:55,470 --> 00:20:57,530
Our ship will be stopping in Yangzhou
for half a day,

292
00:20:57,530 --> 00:20:58,950
so I thought I'd come see you.

293
00:20:58,950 --> 00:20:59,770
And yet here you are,

294
00:20:59,770 --> 00:21:01,430
making me work the whole time.

295
00:21:02,010 --> 00:21:03,360
It's not easy for you
to come all this way.

296
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:05,230
I've got to make the most of it
while you're here.

297
00:21:05,230 --> 00:21:08,260
[Young Wang Jingshu]

298
00:21:09,140 --> 00:21:09,940
Once we part,

299
00:21:10,580 --> 00:21:12,910
who knows when we'll see each other again?

300
00:21:22,550 --> 00:21:23,480
Why wouldn't we?

301
00:21:23,790 --> 00:21:24,900
Didn't we agree

302
00:21:25,010 --> 00:21:26,610
to open a pharmacy together?

303
00:21:26,820 --> 00:21:29,100
When the time comes,

304
00:21:29,250 --> 00:21:30,180
together, we'll

305
00:21:30,350 --> 00:21:35,010
-ease the suffering of women everywhere.
-ease the suffering of women everywhere.

306
00:21:40,770 --> 00:21:42,630
That depends on whether my father

307
00:21:42,700 --> 00:21:45,290
will let me leave the house
when the time comes.

308
00:21:45,290 --> 00:21:46,220
Why wouldn't he?

309
00:21:48,030 --> 00:21:49,420
In families like ours,

310
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:51,120
once a daughter comes of age,

311
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:52,250
many things

312
00:21:52,490 --> 00:21:53,750
are no longer up to her.

313
00:21:57,690 --> 00:21:59,020
Then I'll take you away.

314
00:22:00,030 --> 00:22:01,360
We'll run far, far away,

315
00:22:01,860 --> 00:22:03,920
where your father will never find us.

316
00:22:04,470 --> 00:22:05,250
Jingshu.

317
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:11,030
I know you're unhappy.

318
00:22:12,580 --> 00:22:13,530
And I know

319
00:22:14,630 --> 00:22:16,630
you never wanted this, but...

320
00:22:18,020 --> 00:22:19,950
I shouldn't be saying this, but...

321
00:22:22,550 --> 00:22:24,330
But you deserve to know.

322
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:26,010
You...

323
00:22:26,140 --> 00:22:27,800
It wasn't that old bastard

324
00:22:27,830 --> 00:22:29,480
lying in that grave who chose you,

325
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:30,460
you know?

326
00:22:32,630 --> 00:22:33,690
It was your father.

327
00:22:36,860 --> 00:22:39,120
It was your father who sold you off first.

328
00:23:37,990 --> 00:23:45,420
[In Memory of Celestial Maiden,
Wang Jingshu]

329
00:23:45,450 --> 00:23:47,860
[Vine Roots]

330
00:23:51,860 --> 00:23:52,470
Sister.

331
00:23:54,360 --> 00:23:54,920
Sister?

332
00:23:56,990 --> 00:23:57,720
You're here.

333
00:23:59,010 --> 00:23:59,600
Sister.

334
00:24:00,080 --> 00:24:01,810
Sit down and have a bite with me.

335
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:03,380
Okay.

336
00:24:03,420 --> 00:24:07,800
[Zhang Quan, the Emperor's Brother-in-Law]

337
00:24:03,680 --> 00:24:04,270
Sister.

338
00:24:05,190 --> 00:24:06,590
This is the list of imperial consorts
selected for burial with His Majesty,

339
00:24:06,590 --> 00:24:07,860
drawn up by the Ministry of Rites

340
00:24:07,860 --> 00:24:09,550
in accordance with protocol.

341
00:24:10,210 --> 00:24:12,010
Please review it, Your Majesty.

342
00:24:12,540 --> 00:24:13,540
Who's on the list?

343
00:24:15,710 --> 00:24:17,170
The Palace Women's Bureau

344
00:24:17,320 --> 00:24:19,710
has selected 17 consorts in total.

345
00:24:21,790 --> 00:24:22,790
Three have served

346
00:24:23,010 --> 00:24:24,840
His Majesty for many years,

347
00:24:25,600 --> 00:24:28,800
while another 5 come from
distinguished noble families.

348
00:24:32,230 --> 00:24:33,090
Those families

349
00:24:34,550 --> 00:24:36,550
had already sent word
through intermediaries,

350
00:24:36,550 --> 00:24:37,210
saying that

351
00:24:37,600 --> 00:24:39,270
being buried alongside His Majesty

352
00:24:39,270 --> 00:24:41,530
would bring great honor to their houses,

353
00:24:42,270 --> 00:24:44,490
and that they would be willing
for their daughters

354
00:24:44,490 --> 00:24:46,620
to serve His Majesty for all eternity.

355
00:24:47,160 --> 00:24:48,090
Review the list.

356
00:24:48,290 --> 00:24:49,710
If you have no objections,

357
00:24:49,710 --> 00:24:51,680
I'll proceed according to precedent.

358
00:24:51,680 --> 00:24:52,400
Precedent?

359
00:24:53,120 --> 00:24:56,850
If I recall correctly, you were also
the one who handled everything

360
00:24:57,140 --> 00:24:59,800
when Emperor Taizong passed away,
weren't you?

361
00:25:00,530 --> 00:25:01,120
Yes.

362
00:25:02,780 --> 00:25:07,540
Back then, I personally drew up
the list under imperial orders.

363
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:10,470
The families of those dozen or so consorts
who were buried with him

364
00:25:10,470 --> 00:25:12,360
were all deeply grateful to me.

365
00:25:13,160 --> 00:25:16,360
Many of them have since become
allies of our Zhang family.

366
00:25:19,710 --> 00:25:20,550
What a pity.

367
00:25:21,360 --> 00:25:23,340
These women are all so young.

368
00:25:24,490 --> 00:25:26,550
Their lives cut short in their prime.

369
00:25:36,250 --> 00:25:37,510
What's wrong, Sister?

370
00:25:37,690 --> 00:25:39,290
Are you feeling tired today?

371
00:25:39,750 --> 00:25:42,080
This has been the custom
throughout the dynasties.

372
00:25:42,080 --> 00:25:44,190
Surely we can't let His Majesty

373
00:25:44,220 --> 00:25:45,880
feel lonely in the afterlife, right?

374
00:25:45,880 --> 00:25:46,650
Besides,

375
00:25:47,380 --> 00:25:49,510
having a daughter buried with the Emperor

376
00:25:49,510 --> 00:25:52,990
is an unparalleled honor for any family.

377
00:25:55,250 --> 00:25:56,710
These are troubled times.

378
00:25:57,190 --> 00:26:00,750
Such a practice is bound to
invite criticism

379
00:26:00,900 --> 00:26:03,430
and give people something
to hold against us.

380
00:26:03,510 --> 00:26:04,160
Let's

381
00:26:06,350 --> 00:26:07,770
be prudent this time

382
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:10,300
and keep the numbers down.

383
00:26:11,440 --> 00:26:13,120
The political winds at court are shifting.

384
00:26:13,120 --> 00:26:14,770
I was hoping to use this opportunity

385
00:26:14,770 --> 00:26:15,970
to weed out my enemies

386
00:26:15,990 --> 00:26:17,190
and win over a few more allies.

387
00:26:17,190 --> 00:26:19,250
I've said it. Keep the death toll low.

388
00:26:22,700 --> 00:26:24,360
That's always the right call.

389
00:26:26,700 --> 00:26:27,300
All right.

390
00:26:27,930 --> 00:26:29,830
[One Imperial Consort: Consort Guo]

391
00:26:42,350 --> 00:26:43,550
That's settled then.

392
00:26:44,630 --> 00:26:46,630
Go ahead and make the arrangements.

393
00:26:55,160 --> 00:26:55,790
By the way,

394
00:26:58,140 --> 00:26:59,940
I don't care what method you use,

395
00:27:01,530 --> 00:27:02,990
but before His Majesty...

396
00:27:04,890 --> 00:27:06,690
Before His Majesty passes away,

397
00:27:08,070 --> 00:27:10,130
you must bring the Crown Prince back.

398
00:27:10,790 --> 00:27:11,520
Understood?

399
00:27:15,530 --> 00:27:17,390
I understand what you're saying.

400
00:27:18,470 --> 00:27:19,270
But what if...

401
00:27:19,340 --> 00:27:21,600
What if my nephew has already
met with some misfortune,

402
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:23,200
-you...
-Slap your own face!

403
00:27:25,570 --> 00:27:26,830
You still don't get it.

404
00:27:30,470 --> 00:27:32,180
All you do is talk about him
being in danger

405
00:27:32,180 --> 00:27:33,550
or meeting some misfortune.

406
00:27:33,550 --> 00:27:36,080
Can't you say something auspicious
for once?

407
00:27:37,730 --> 00:27:38,750
I'll say it again:

408
00:27:40,340 --> 00:27:41,670
bring the Crown Prince—

409
00:27:42,420 --> 00:27:46,790
I said, bring the Crown Prince back.

410
00:30:45,730 --> 00:30:46,600
Pardon me.

411
00:31:32,040 --> 00:31:32,710
Stop there.

412
00:31:33,620 --> 00:31:34,270
You.

413
00:31:37,590 --> 00:31:39,120
What's your business here?

414
00:31:42,950 --> 00:31:45,010
Speak up! Has the cat got your tongue?

415
00:31:46,550 --> 00:31:47,950
Well, Liu is sick.

416
00:31:48,090 --> 00:31:51,070
The village chief sent me
to look after him.

417
00:31:51,380 --> 00:31:52,640
Look after him?

418
00:31:52,670 --> 00:31:54,710
He's dead! What is there to look after?

419
00:31:54,710 --> 00:31:55,640
Get off the boat.

420
00:31:57,230 --> 00:31:57,750
Bro.

421
00:31:57,880 --> 00:31:59,950
It... It was the village chief
who told me to come look after him.

422
00:31:59,950 --> 00:32:00,640
I told you to get off.

423
00:32:00,640 --> 00:32:01,700
Didn't you hear me?

424
00:32:04,290 --> 00:32:04,820
Alright.

425
00:32:10,940 --> 00:32:11,740
Come on. Here.

426
00:32:12,440 --> 00:32:13,040
Come here.

427
00:32:14,950 --> 00:32:15,600
Come on.

428
00:32:15,750 --> 00:32:16,480
A bit closer.

429
00:32:18,920 --> 00:32:20,530
You dare to act tough with me, huh?

430
00:32:20,530 --> 00:32:21,640
Do you know who I am?

431
00:32:21,670 --> 00:32:22,560
Kneel down!

432
00:32:32,590 --> 00:32:34,050
Acting tough with me, huh?

433
00:32:58,940 --> 00:33:00,400
Still trying to get up?

434
00:33:00,500 --> 00:33:01,420
Come on!

435
00:33:16,230 --> 00:33:17,630
Still acting tough, huh?

436
00:33:44,440 --> 00:33:45,120
Fine.

437
00:33:48,140 --> 00:33:50,330
This is what you get for acting tough
in front of me!

438
00:33:50,330 --> 00:33:51,480
Screw you!

439
00:34:03,320 --> 00:34:04,780
You better remember this:

440
00:34:05,160 --> 00:34:05,890
around here,

441
00:34:06,380 --> 00:34:07,710
I'm the boss.

442
00:34:40,070 --> 00:34:41,600
T-Two of you, get over here.

443
00:34:41,730 --> 00:34:42,940
Dispose of that body.

444
00:34:43,100 --> 00:34:43,630
Yes, sir.

445
00:34:44,340 --> 00:34:45,630
If Officer Xue sees it,

446
00:34:46,469 --> 00:34:48,130
he'll give us another earful.

447
00:34:48,780 --> 00:34:49,360
Fall in.

448
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:51,199
M-Move out!

449
00:35:10,470 --> 00:35:14,430
[Huai'an]

450
00:35:24,360 --> 00:35:25,090
This guy

451
00:35:25,460 --> 00:35:27,060
actually had 2 steamed buns.

452
00:35:46,790 --> 00:35:47,790
Here, yours.

453
00:35:50,200 --> 00:35:50,860
Careful.

454
00:35:51,740 --> 00:35:52,340
Next.

455
00:35:55,910 --> 00:35:56,470
Alright.

456
00:35:58,970 --> 00:35:59,570
Careful.

457
00:36:00,580 --> 00:36:01,210
Next.

458
00:36:03,380 --> 00:36:04,010
Hurry up.

459
00:36:08,820 --> 00:36:09,370
Okay.

460
00:36:12,810 --> 00:36:14,070
One more bowl, please.

461
00:36:18,300 --> 00:36:19,830
Bro, a little more, please.

462
00:36:22,330 --> 00:36:22,960
Thank you.

463
00:36:47,050 --> 00:36:52,380
[Kong Shiba, Tracker]

464
00:36:51,220 --> 00:36:52,050
Young man,

465
00:36:52,770 --> 00:36:54,230
where did you pop out from?

466
00:37:09,650 --> 00:37:10,490
Bro...

467
00:37:13,880 --> 00:37:14,820
Buddies,

468
00:37:15,740 --> 00:37:17,530
that ship just crashed.

469
00:37:17,560 --> 00:37:20,230
Have you all been standing here
watching this whole time?

470
00:37:20,230 --> 00:37:22,030
What else were we supposed to do?

471
00:37:32,090 --> 00:37:32,860
So, bro,

472
00:37:35,370 --> 00:37:38,230
are there any survivors?

473
00:37:38,990 --> 00:37:39,650
Survivors?

474
00:37:44,110 --> 00:37:46,770
That 400-liao grain ship
was smashed to pieces.

475
00:37:46,920 --> 00:37:49,590
The people aboard must be nothing
but mangled flesh by now.

476
00:37:49,590 --> 00:37:51,390
How could anyone have survived?

477
00:37:57,990 --> 00:37:59,340
Come on. Eat up.

478
00:38:42,870 --> 00:38:43,740
Rectifier Yu.

479
00:38:46,010 --> 00:38:47,050
Let me ask you,

480
00:38:48,020 --> 00:38:49,620
can you protect me all the way

481
00:38:50,770 --> 00:38:51,790
to Beijing?

482
00:38:54,200 --> 00:38:56,090
But if we all work together,

483
00:38:57,530 --> 00:38:58,570
maybe we can do it.

484
00:39:40,320 --> 00:39:41,520
To be honest with you,

485
00:39:41,570 --> 00:39:43,010
I'm passing through Huai'an on a mission

486
00:39:43,010 --> 00:39:44,330
from the imperial palace in Jinling.

487
00:39:44,330 --> 00:39:46,460
I'm delivering a confidential report

488
00:39:48,940 --> 00:39:50,010
to Beijing.

489
00:39:50,610 --> 00:39:51,340
But somehow,

490
00:39:51,920 --> 00:39:54,110
the report went missing on that ship.

491
00:39:54,340 --> 00:39:55,290
I've been searching everywhere,

492
00:39:55,290 --> 00:39:57,850
and l-look at the state I'm in now.

493
00:39:58,280 --> 00:39:59,850
But I still haven't found it.

494
00:39:59,850 --> 00:40:02,840
A confidential report
from the Jinling imperial palace?

495
00:40:02,840 --> 00:40:03,380
Yes.

496
00:40:04,800 --> 00:40:07,380
If it fell into the hands of
those trackers,

497
00:40:07,740 --> 00:40:09,550
there's no way you'd ever find it again.

498
00:40:09,550 --> 00:40:10,240
Exactly.

499
00:40:11,260 --> 00:40:12,050
That's why

500
00:40:13,260 --> 00:40:16,920
I'd like to ask you, Fang, to lead
some men and help me search for it.

501
00:40:17,760 --> 00:40:19,590
Tingyi, there's something
you don't understand.

502
00:40:19,590 --> 00:40:21,070
The canal

503
00:40:21,090 --> 00:40:22,760
falls under the jurisdiction of
the Canal Transport Office.

504
00:40:22,760 --> 00:40:24,110
I'm with the Huai'an Branch
of the Ministry of Justice.

505
00:40:24,110 --> 00:40:25,880
If I overstep my authority,

506
00:40:26,380 --> 00:40:29,450
the other judicial commissioners
will only make things difficult for me.

507
00:40:29,450 --> 00:40:30,260
Fang,

508
00:40:31,360 --> 00:40:32,970
didn't you just say

509
00:40:33,110 --> 00:40:34,450
you wanted to serve the imperial court?

510
00:40:34,450 --> 00:40:37,510
Are you going to back down
at the first little obstacle?

511
00:40:37,900 --> 00:40:38,820
You can't do that.

512
00:40:38,820 --> 00:40:39,590
If you act like that,

513
00:40:39,590 --> 00:40:41,350
how are you any different
from those judicial commissioners

514
00:40:41,350 --> 00:40:42,300
you were just criticizing,

515
00:40:42,300 --> 00:40:42,900
right?

516
00:40:43,150 --> 00:40:45,010
It's not that I don't want to help.

517
00:40:45,160 --> 00:40:46,670
It's just that things along the canal

518
00:40:46,670 --> 00:40:47,970
are extremely complicated.

519
00:40:47,970 --> 00:40:50,760
The court has been talking about
abolishing the canal transport system

520
00:40:50,760 --> 00:40:52,300
and moving the capital for ages.
But now, no one knows when it'll happen,

521
00:40:52,300 --> 00:40:54,220
and canal transport can't stop
in the meantime.

522
00:40:54,220 --> 00:40:56,570
So they've had to resume the process
of hauling boats over the dams.

523
00:40:56,570 --> 00:40:57,090
Tingyi,

524
00:40:57,220 --> 00:40:57,940
you know that

525
00:40:57,940 --> 00:41:00,150
this requires conscripted laborers
to pull the tow ropes.

526
00:41:00,150 --> 00:41:02,020
But with the summer harvest approaching,

527
00:41:02,020 --> 00:41:04,020
no one is willing to do unpaid labor.

528
00:41:05,300 --> 00:41:06,900
It's a vicious cycle.

529
00:41:07,130 --> 00:41:08,170
The fewer laborers there are,

530
00:41:08,170 --> 00:41:10,450
the harder the authorities
push the remaining ones,

531
00:41:10,450 --> 00:41:12,050
and the more resentment the trackers feel.

532
00:41:12,050 --> 00:41:13,440
That's why no one in the yamen

533
00:41:13,440 --> 00:41:15,200
wants to get involved in this mess
right now.

534
00:41:15,200 --> 00:41:16,670
Alright, alright, I get it.

535
00:41:16,670 --> 00:41:17,730
No need to say more.

536
00:41:18,110 --> 00:41:18,910
I understand.

537
00:41:19,470 --> 00:41:21,600
Better to play it safe than take risks.

538
00:41:22,730 --> 00:41:23,460
That's fine.

539
00:41:23,900 --> 00:41:25,160
If you can't handle it,

540
00:41:25,400 --> 00:41:27,000
I'll find someone who can.

541
00:41:27,660 --> 00:41:28,300
Wait!

542
00:41:31,340 --> 00:41:32,940
I never said I wouldn't help.

543
00:41:34,300 --> 00:41:35,530
Our Huai'an Branch

544
00:41:35,820 --> 00:41:37,090
of the Ministry of Justice

545
00:41:37,090 --> 00:41:39,800
may not have direct jurisdiction
over canal affairs,

546
00:41:39,800 --> 00:41:41,630
but if people are gathering
to cause trouble,

547
00:41:41,630 --> 00:41:44,150
or if it even involves treasonous factions
stirring up trouble,

548
00:41:44,150 --> 00:41:45,490
then given the sudden nature of this,

549
00:41:45,490 --> 00:41:47,900
it's absolutely my duty
as a judicial commissioner

550
00:41:47,900 --> 00:41:49,230
to investigate.

551
00:41:57,520 --> 00:41:58,840
Even back in our school days,

552
00:41:58,840 --> 00:42:01,340
I noticed that you were
the most meticulous thinker.

553
00:42:01,340 --> 00:42:01,930
That makes every sense.

554
00:42:01,930 --> 00:42:03,780
Out of all the grain ships out there,

555
00:42:03,780 --> 00:42:05,200
why did the one I was on

556
00:42:05,200 --> 00:42:06,550
happen to have its mooring rope snap?

557
00:42:06,550 --> 00:42:08,570
If someone deliberately sabotaged it,

558
00:42:08,570 --> 00:42:10,570
they must have been after
that confidential report I was carrying.

559
00:42:10,570 --> 00:42:11,170
Very well.

560
00:42:11,720 --> 00:42:13,160
I'll mobilize the troops right away.

561
00:42:13,160 --> 00:42:13,800
Okay.

562
00:42:57,600 --> 00:42:58,420
You're awake.

563
00:42:59,010 --> 00:43:00,610
You sure slept soundly, kid.

564
00:43:01,420 --> 00:43:02,550
I'm almost jealous.

565
00:43:07,670 --> 00:43:09,290
Must be the extra meal
for the night shift.
